L = dict(title='Unit 4: Software Testing', points=[
 'Error is human galti, fault is the bug in code, failure is the wrong behaviour the user sees: Error to Fault to Failure',
 'Verification asks are we building the product right, it is static, uses reviews and inspections, no code runs',
 'Validation asks are we building the right product, it is dynamic, code is executed with test cases',
 'Levels of testing: unit, integration, system, acceptance. Integration can be top down, bottom up, big bang or sandwich',
 'White box testing looks inside the code, black box testing checks only inputs and outputs',
 'Cyclomatic complexity V of G equals E minus N plus 2, or P plus 1, or number of regions',
 'V of G is the number of independent paths, so you need at least that many test cases',
 'Boundary value analysis: min minus, min, min plus, nominal, max minus, max, max plus. Normal BVA gives 4n plus 1 cases, robust gives 6n plus 1',
 'Equivalence class testing: split input into valid and invalid classes and test one value from each class',
 'Decision table: conditions on top, actions below, every column is a rule and one test case. TDD cycle is Red, Green, Refactor'], scenes=[
 S('Namaste doston! Gussa Guru yahan. Aaj Unit four, Software Testing, jahan sabse zyada numericals aate hain. Pehle ek chhoti kahani. Angry Birds mein tumne pig ko galat angle se target kiya. Yeh tumhari galti hai, isko error bolte hain. Is galti ki wajah se code mein ek bug ban gaya, isko fault bolte hain. Aur jab bird pig tak pahuncha hi nahi, yeh failure hai. Yaad rakho, Error se Fault, Fault se Failure.',
  'Error (galti) -> Fault (bug) -> Failure (galat output). Teeno alag hain!',
  [['h', 'Unit 4 map'], ['row', ['Error', 'Fault', 'Failure']], ['row', ['Verification', 'Validation', 'Levels']], ['row', ['White box', 'Black box', 'TDD']], ['t', 'Numericals: cyclomatic complexity, BVA, discount test cases.']],
  []),
 S('Ab verification versus validation, yeh end sem ka question hai. Verification ka matlab hai, kya hum product sahi tarah bana rahe hain? Isme code chalta hi nahi, sirf documents aur code padhte hain, review, walkthrough, inspection. Validation ka matlab hai, kya hum sahi product bana rahe hain? Isme code run karke test cases se check karte hain. Test case design methods jaise black box aur white box mainly validation mein use hote hain. Testing strategy dono ko milake ek overall plan banati hai.',
  'Verification = padhna (static). Validation = chalana (dynamic).',
  [['h', 'Verification vs Validation'], ['tbl', [['Point', 'Verification', 'Validation'], ['Question', 'Product sahi bana?', 'Sahi product bana?'], ['Type', 'Static, no execution', 'Dynamic, code runs'], ['Methods', 'Review, walkthrough, inspection', 'Black box, white box tests'], ['Who', 'QA team, peers', 'Testers'], ['Time', 'Early, before coding', 'After code is ready']]], ['t', 'Trick: Verification = Verify papers. Validation = Value for user (use it).']],
  []),
 S('Testing ke levels yaad karo. Sabse chhota unit testing, ek ek module ko alag test karna. Phir integration testing, modules ko jodkar dekhna. Phir system testing, poora software ek saath. Aakhir mein acceptance testing, jahan customer khud check karta hai. Alpha testing developer ke ghar par, beta testing customer ke ghar par. Integration ke chaar tareeke hain: top down, bottom up, big bang aur sandwich.',
  'Unit -> Integration -> System -> Acceptance. Chhote se bade tak!',
  [['h', 'Levels of testing (V shape)'], ['col', ['Acceptance testing (customer, alpha/beta)', 'System testing (whole software)', 'Integration testing (modules joined)', 'Unit testing (single module)']], ['tbl', [['Integration type', 'Idea'], ['Top down', 'Main first, stubs for lower modules'], ['Bottom up', 'Low modules first, drivers on top'], ['Big bang', 'Join everything at once'], ['Sandwich', 'Top down + bottom up together']]]],
  []),
 S('Ab white box testing. Isme tester code ke andar dekhta hai, jaise glass ka dabba. Coverage ke chaar type: statement, branch, condition, path. Pehla chhota numerical dekho. Agar program mein das statements hain aur tumhare test cases se aath chale, to statement coverage kitna hua? Executed divided by total into hundred.',
  'Coverage % = executed / total x 100',
  [['h', 'White box = glass box'], ['tbl', [['Coverage', 'Matlab'], ['Statement', 'Har line kam se kam ek baar chale'], ['Branch', 'Har if ke True aur False dono chalein'], ['Condition', 'Har condition True aur False'], ['Path', 'Har possible raasta chale']]], ['t', 'Black box = bina andar dekhe sirf input aur output check.']],
  ['## Statement coverage', '? 10 statements, 8 executed', 'Coverage = 8 / 10 x 100', '! Statement coverage = 80 percent', '## Branch coverage', '? 6 branches, 4 taken', 'Coverage = 4 / 6 x 100', '! Branch coverage = 66.7 percent', '~ Branch coverage is stronger than statement']),
 S('Ab sabse important numerical, cyclomatic complexity. Pehle control flow graph banao. Har statement ya block ek node, aur jaane ka raasta ek edge. Quadratic equation program lete hain, jo lab mein bhi hai. Pehle a barabar zero check, phir discriminant d nikalo, phir d zero, d positive ya negative. Teen decision hain.',
  'Flow graph: Node = statement, Edge = raasta, Predicate = decision',
  [['h', 'Control flow graph: quadratic program'], ['graph', {'1': [0.50, 0.06, '1 read a,b,c', 'b'], '2': [0.50, 0.24, '2 a==0?', 'd'], '3': [0.14, 0.42, '3 Not quadratic', 'b'], '4': [0.66, 0.42, '4 d=b*b-4ac', 'b'], '5': [0.66, 0.60, '5 d==0?', 'd'], '6': [0.36, 0.76, '6 Equal', 'b'], '7': [0.86, 0.76, '7 d>0?', 'd'], '8': [0.70, 0.94, '8 Real', 'b'], '9': [0.96, 0.94, '9 Imag', 'b']}, [['1', '2', ''], ['2', '3', 'T'], ['2', '4', 'F'], ['4', '5', ''], ['5', '6', 'T'], ['5', '7', 'F'], ['7', '8', 'T'], ['7', '9', 'F']], 330]],
  ['## Cyclomatic complexity V(G)', 'Formula 1: V(G) = E - N + 2', 'Nodes N = 10 (with end node)', 'Edges E = 12', 'V(G) = 12 - 10 + 2 = 4', 'Formula 2: V(G) = P + 1', 'Predicate nodes P = 3', 'V(G) = 3 + 1 = 4', 'Formula 3: V(G) = regions = 4', '! V(G) = 4 -> 4 independent paths', '## Independent paths', 'P1: 1-2-3-end', 'P2: 1-2-4-5-6-end', 'P3: 1-2-4-5-7-8-end', 'P4: 1-2-4-5-7-9-end']),
 S('Ab test cases nikalte hain. Chaar independent paths hain, to kam se kam chaar test cases chahiye. Path one ke liye a zero do, to Not a quadratic equation. Path two ke liye one, two, one do, discriminant zero, Equal roots. Path three ke liye one, five, two, discriminant seventeen, Real roots. Path four ke liye five, one, two, discriminant negative, Imaginary roots. Do more numericals: agar edges seventeen aur nodes thirteen hain, to V G kitna?',
  'V(G) paths = minimum test cases. Mini numericals bhi kar lo!',
  [['h', 'Test cases from paths'], ['tbl', [['Path', 'a, b, c', 'Expected'], ['P1', '0, 5, 3', 'Not a quadratic equation'], ['P2', '1, 2, 1', 'Equal roots'], ['P3', '1, 5, 2', 'Real roots'], ['P4', '5, 1, 2', 'Imaginary roots']]], ['t', 'Check: P3 d = 25 - 8 = 17 > 0. P4 d = 1 - 40 = -39 < 0.']],
  ['## Mini numerical 1', '? E = 17, N = 13', 'V(G) = E - N + 2', 'V(G) = 17 - 13 + 2', '! V(G) = 6', '## Mini numerical 2', '? Code has if, while, if', 'P = 3', 'V(G) = 3 + 1', '! V(G) = 4', '~ Loop condition also counts as predicate']),
 S('Ab PYQ four c, credit card discount scenario. Teen conditions hain. New customer ko fifteen percent. Existing customer jiske paas loyalty card hai ko ten percent. Coupon hai to twenty percent, lekin new customer ke saath coupon nahi chalega. Discount jud jaate hain. Isko code ki tarah socho: teen if. To teen decisions, V G barabar four. Ab har raaste ke liye test case likho.',
  '3 decisions -> V(G) = 4 -> test cases likho, coupon + new = refuse!',
  [['h', 'Discount logic as flow'], ['graph', {'s': [0.50, 0.05, 'Start', 'o'], 'a': [0.50, 0.24, 'New customer?', 'd'], 'a1': [0.88, 0.24, '+15%', 'b'], 'b': [0.50, 0.50, 'Existing + loyalty?', 'd'], 'b1': [0.88, 0.50, '+10%', 'b'], 'c': [0.50, 0.76, 'Coupon and NOT new?', 'd'], 'c1': [0.88, 0.76, '+20%', 'b'], 'e': [0.50, 0.96, 'Total discount', 'o']}, [['s', 'a', ''], ['a', 'a1', 'Y'], ['a', 'b', 'N'], ['a1', 'b', ''], ['b', 'b1', 'Y'], ['b', 'c', 'N'], ['b1', 'c', ''], ['c', 'c1', 'Y'], ['c', 'e', 'N'], ['c1', 'e', '']], 340]],
  ['## White box test cases', 'V(G) = 3 decisions + 1 = 4', '(strict, 5 conditions: 5 + 1 = 6)', 'TC1: new, no coupon -> 15%', 'TC2: existing + loyalty -> 10%', 'TC3: existing, coupon, no loyalty -> 20%', 'TC4: existing + loyalty + coupon -> 30%', 'TC5: new + coupon -> 15% (coupon refused)', 'TC6: existing, no loyalty, no coupon -> 0%', '! 4 paths minimum, 6 cases cover all branches', '~ Discounts are added: 10 + 20 = 30']),
 S('Ab black box, pehla tool boundary value analysis. Galtiyan zyada tar boundary par hoti hain, jaise less than ki jagah less than equal. Isliye min, min plus one, nominal, max minus one, max, aur robust mein min minus one aur max plus one bhi test karte hain. Quadratic program mein teen inputs hain, a b c, har ek one se hundred. Normal BVA mein four n plus one, yaani thirteen test cases. Robust mein six n plus one, yaani nineteen. Nominal fifty lete hain.',
  'Normal BVA = 4n+1. Robust BVA = 6n+1. n = number of inputs',
  [['h', 'BVA number line (range 1 to 100)'], ['row', ['min-1 = 0', 'min = 1', 'min+1 = 2', 'nom = 50']], ['row', ['max-1 = 99', 'max = 100', 'max+1 = 101']], ['tbl', [['Type', 'Formula', 'n = 3'], ['Normal BVA', '4n + 1', '13'], ['Robust BVA', '6n + 1', '19'], ['Worst case', '5 to the power n', '125'], ['Robust worst', '7 to the power n', '343']]], ['t', 'Normal skips min-1 and max+1. Robust adds both.']],
  ['## Normal BVA, 13 cases (a, b, c)', 'vary a: (1,50,50) Real | (2,50,50) Real', '(99,50,50) Imag | (100,50,50) Imag', 'vary b: (50,1,50) Imag | (50,2,50) Imag', '(50,99,50) Imag | (50,100,50) Equal', 'vary c: (50,50,1) Real | (50,50,2) Real', '(50,50,99) Imag | (50,50,100) Imag', 'nominal: (50,50,50) Imag', '! 4 x 3 + 1 = 13 cases', '## Robust adds 6 more', 'a=0, a=101, b=0, b=101, c=0, c=101', '~ Out of range -> Invalid input (a=0 may be Not quadratic)', '? Single input age 18 to 60', '! Test 17, 18, 19, 39, 59, 60, 61']),
 S('Ab equivalence class testing aur decision table. Equivalence class mein input ko valid aur invalid groups mein baant do, aur har group se sirf ek value test karo. Jaise age eighteen se sixty: valid group eighteen se sixty, invalid group less than eighteen aur more than sixty. Decision table mein conditions upar, actions neeche, aur har column ek rule, yaani ek test case. Discount scenario ko decision table mein dekho. Cause effect graph isi table ka picture hai, aur state table testing mein states aur events ki table se test cases banate hain.',
  'Equivalence = ek group se ek test. Decision table = har rule ek test',
  [['h', 'Decision table: discount'], ['tbl', [['Rule', 'New', 'Loyal', 'Coupon', 'Discount'], ['R1', 'Y', 'N', 'N', '15'], ['R2', 'Y', 'N', 'Y', '15'], ['R3', 'N', 'Y', 'N', '10'], ['R4', 'N', 'Y', 'Y', '30'], ['R5', 'N', 'N', 'Y', '20'], ['R6', 'N', 'N', 'N', '0']]], ['t', 'New + Loyal both Y is impossible, so it is dropped. 6 rules = 6 tests.']],
  ['## Equivalence classes', '? Age field valid 18 to 60', 'Class 1 invalid: age < 18 -> test 10', 'Class 2 valid: 18 to 60 -> test 35', 'Class 3 invalid: age > 60 -> test 70', '! 3 classes = 3 test cases', '~ BVA then adds 17, 18, 60, 61']),
 S('Last mein agile testing aur TDD. Test Driven Development ka cycle: Red, Green, Refactor. Red matlab pehle failing test likho. Green matlab bas itna code likho ki test pass ho jaye. Refactor matlab code ko saaf karo. Angry Birds jaisa: pehle shot lagao, miss hua, red. Angle theek kiya, hit hua, green. Phir shot ko perfect karo, refactor. Agile testing mein testing sprint ke saath saath chalti hai, aakhir mein nahi. Agile quadrants mein unit tests, functional tests, exploratory tests aur performance security tests aate hain.',
  'TDD: Red (fail) -> Green (pass) -> Refactor (clean). Testing sprint ke saath!',
  [['h', 'TDD cycle'], ['row', ['RED: write failing test', 'GREEN: make it pass', 'REFACTOR: clean code']], ['tbl', [['Agile quadrant', 'Tests'], ['Q1', 'Unit, component (developers)'], ['Q2', 'Functional, acceptance (business)'], ['Q3', 'Exploratory, usability'], ['Q4', 'Performance, security']]], ['t', 'Whole team tests. Continuous testing with every build.']],
  []),
])
